  "notes": "Piano solo on ONE grand staff (brace). A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" with 2 staves; it must NOT be split into right/left hand parts, and the second right-hand voice in bars 13-16 must stay inside the piano part (voice 2), not become a new part. DAMAGE (photocopy-thin): Light photocopy, 1-bit: low binarisation threshold so only the darkest ink survives - staff lines, stems, ledger lines, slurs and hollow noteheads thin out and break up. mild thr 115, scan thr 85, severe thr 70 + patchy faded ink + 0.6 deg skew + toner dust. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Severe: some staff-line segments, ledger lines, ties and lyric hyphens/extenders vanish completely; the truth still contains them."
